  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "CH06129",
    "sub_id": "97459",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>本課程採取多元評量方式，結合個人表現與團隊協作，重點在於理論的理解、工具的應用以及實作的反思。</div>\n\n<div><strong>1. 參與與課堂討論 (20%)：VT 思維紀錄15%+出席紀錄5%</strong></div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>說明：</strong>&nbsp;針對課堂中進行的教學法分析與新聞討論，每組需記錄運用&nbsp;<strong>VT 工具 (如 See-Think-Wonder, Connect-Extend-Challenge)</strong>&nbsp;的討論過程與結果。</li>\n\t<li><strong>評分重點：</strong>&nbsp;討論的深度、是否正確運用 VT 工具引導思維、組員間的溝通互動。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div><strong>2. 學生學習筆記 (10%)</strong></div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>說明：</strong>&nbsp;學生需在平時課堂中整理個人學習筆記。此筆記將作為<strong>期中測驗時唯一的 Open Book 參考來源</strong>。</li>\n\t<li><strong>評分重點：</strong>&nbsp;內容完整度（涵蓋 Ch 1-11）、邏輯條理、是否有個人反思紀錄。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div><strong>3. 期中測驗 (30%)：核心概念辨析</strong></div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>計分比例：</strong>&nbsp;<strong>小組分數 40% / 個人分數 60%</strong>。</li>\n\t<li><strong>形式：</strong>&nbsp;開放筆記 (Open Book) 測驗。包含小組共同解決的教學情境題，以及個人對教學法理論的理解。</li>\n\t<li><strong>範圍：</strong>&nbsp;Textbook Chapters 1&ndash;11。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div><strong>4. 出席 (10%)</strong></div>\n\n<div><strong>5. 期末專題發表 (30%)</strong></div>\n\n<div><br />\n&nbsp;</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "1. Be on time. 請準時到課。\n2. Participate in the class discussion and class activities. 請參與課堂討論及課堂活動。\n3. Students must submit a leave application to the school in advance, stating the reason for the leave and the expected duration.學生必須提前向學校提交請假申請，說明請假的原因和預計時間。\n4. Please purchase original textbook, following intellectual property law. 請購買正版課本，請勿使用複製版本。\n5. The texts and exercises will be completed in class. Please bring textbooks to class. 請上課攜帶課本，以利上課活動使用。\n6. Follow the school rules to apply for a make-up exam within three days of the exam date. Relevant documents are required for the application. No-shows or those with late application will receive ZERO. The date of a make-up exam will be arranged by the instructor. 若須要補考的同學，請遵照學校的補考規定，在考試後的3天內提出申請。若考試當天沒有出現或者是沒有申請補考的同學，考試成績一律0分。\n7. Following the FCU Exam Regulations, cheaters will receive ZERO for their exams and such cases will be reviewed by the Student Reward and Disciplinary Committee. 考試請遵照考場規定，若作弊者以0分計算。\n8.本課程從109學年度起，廣泛閱讀的評分將主要依據Xreading系統所累進的字數而定。學生可與授課教師協調，以其他方式進行廣泛閱讀、檢核其學習成效，但進行方式須符合廣泛閱讀之精神並有客觀閱讀之事實。Starting from the 2020-2021 academic year, extensive reading (ER) will be mainly based on the word count accumulated on the Xreading platform over the semester. An alternative plan proposed by students, if approved by their teacher, may be acceptable. However, the alternative must be in compliance with the tenants of ER. Students need to present evidence to demonstrate that they have met the requirements as agreed to by their teachers.",
    "course_pol_en": null,
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<ol>\n\t<li>Students must exhibit honesty and ethical behavior in their academic activities, avoiding plagiarism and falsification of data.學生在學術活動中必須展現誠實和道德行為，避免抄襲和篡改資料。</li>\n\t<li>Plagiarism: Proper citation of sources is required. Copying or using others&#39; work without appropriate attribution is considered plagiarism.抄襲：必須適當引用來源。未經適當標示使用他人作品屬於抄襲行為。</li>\n\t<li>Cheating: Following exam rules is mandatory. Unauthorized materials or collusion with others during exams is considered cheating.考試作弊：必須遵守考試規則，禁止使用未經授權的材料或與他人串通作弊。</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": null,
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
